  {
   "title": null,
   "text": "Avatar is a Box with the following properties preset. You can customize it using the properties available in Box.\n\n- align: `\"center\"`\n- justify: `\"center\"`\n- overflow: `\"hidden\"`\n- round: `\"full\"`",
   "format": "md"
  },
  {
   "title": "React/DOM Properties",
   "text": "At its core, the Avatar component is a regular <div> element. Thus, both DOM and React properties, methods, and events are accessible. To read up on all of the possible DOM attributes and types available for div elements, check out this [MDN Web Documents page.](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/div) To learn more about DOM events and methods, you can read more on the [MDN Web Events documentation page](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Events).\n\nAlso, feel free to read about the [types of React events available](https://reactjs.org/docs/handling-events.html), or see [how DOM attributes change in React.](https://reactjs.org/docs/dom-elements.html) Working in tandem with Styled Components, you also have access to the [as property.](https://styled-components.com/docs/api#as-polymorphic-prop)",
   "format": "md"
  }
 ],
